![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The JSON pointer generated by `indexedRef` defaults to `/rows/${index}`. However, in the full production receipts file (`source-visual-receipts-production-full-858.v1.json`), the array containing these row references is named `full_row_refs` instead of `rows`. This results in an invalid JSON pointer `/rows/${index}` being generated for `source_visual_receipt_full_row_ref` in the production index.

We should override the `json_pointer` and `selector` properties by passing them in the `extra` parameter of `indexedRef` to ensure the pointer correctly resolves to `/full_row_refs/${index}`.

```javascript
      ...(scope === 'full_858'
        ? {
            source_visual_receipt_full_row_ref: indexedRef(
              paths.sourceVisualReceiptsProductionIn,
              cropQaInfo.index,
              questionKey,
              {
                json_pointer: `/full_row_refs/${cropQaInfo.index}`,
                selector: {
                  full_row_refs_match: {
                    question_key: questionKey,
                  },
                },
              }
            )
          }
        : {}),
```
